      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A total of 1276 schoolchildren aged 11-17 from a Moscow district have been examined. 1172 subjects underwent a complete program examination including biochemical investigation of blood (78.9% of all the children to be examined or 95% of all the schoolchildren examined). The occurrence of combined basic indices, known as adult risk factors of coronary heart disease has been studied in each age and sex group of this population. The data obtained can be used in the differential approach to the planning of preventive measures at the population level."},
